# Channel Club configuration, read by run.sh and Docker Compose.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything here is optional for Docker: leave a setting commented out and set
# it in the app instead (the first-run wizard at /setup, later Admin Panel ›
# Server). A setting made here wins and locks its group in the app. Any auth
# setting below closes the wizard for good, so set all of sign-in here or none.
#
# Only what a deploy sets is listed here. Tuned defaults (media limits, HLS and
# highlight timings, temp dirs, feedback rate limits, body caps) live in the
# Advanced block of backend/app/config.py; override one by its upper-case name.
# The frontend build takes no configuration, so there are no VITE_ variables.

# --- Authentication -----------------------------------------------------------
# Leave this whole block commented out to set up sign-in in the app.

# Token signing key. Optional: without it, one is generated at first start and
# saved in /data/settings.json. Generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32`;
# startup refuses anything under 32 characters.
# JWT_SECRET=

# Local username/password login. A blank password disables that account.
# LOCAL_AUTH_ENABLED=true
# ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# VIEWER_USERNAME=viewer
# VIEWER_PASSWORD=

# Plex login. PLEX_SERVER_MACHINE_ID is required when it is on.
# PLEX_AUTH_ENABLED=true
# PLEX_SERVER_MACHINE_ID=
# Optional: lets the server owner in as admin
# PLEX_SERVER_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated Plex usernames who get the admin role
# PLEX_ADMIN_USERS_STR=

# --- Sources ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neither URL has a default; startup names any that is unset.

# Dispatcharr. The server calls its API here and browsers play streams from it,
# so it must be reachable from both.
# DISPATCHARR_URL=https://dispatcharr.example.com
# Personal API key from the Dispatcharr profile page
# DISPATCHARR_API_KEY=

# ErsatzTV, only if used. Its M3U and XMLTV feeds are found under this URL.
# ERSATZTV_BASE_URL=http://ersatztv.example.com:8409

# --- Features (all off by default) ----------------------------------------------

# CHAT_ENABLED=true
# GIFs in chat are on when a Giphy key is set (developers.giphy.com)
# GIPHY_API_KEY=

# Highlight capture (FFmpeg is in the image). Chromecast is always on.
# HIGHLIGHT_ENABLED=true

# Clip uploads to a shared Zipline account (needs HIGHLIGHT_ENABLED).
# Instance base URL, without /api/upload. Backend only; never a VITE_ variable.
# ZIPLINE_ENABLED=true
# ZIPLINE_URL=https://clips.example.com
# ZIPLINE_TOKEN=

# Live NHL scores over the player, and which channel carries each game
# NHL_ENABLED=true

# Feedback button that pushes to an ntfy topic. Backend only; never VITE_.
# NTFY_ENABLED=true
# NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh
# NTFY_TOPIC=channel-club-feedback
# Only for protected topics
# NTFY_TOKEN=

# --- Logging ------------------------------------------------------------------

# The log level can also be set in the app (Advanced)
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# json for Loki, pretty for a terminal
LOG_FORMAT=pretty
